cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying manuscript, please cite it as below."
title: "Fail-Safe Context-Adaptive Access Control with Continuous Risk Belief Updates and Hard Safety Invariants for Cyber-Physical IoT"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Aljawarneh
    given-names: Mahmoud
    email: ma_jawarneh@asu.edu.jo
    affiliation: "Department of Cybersecurity and Cloud Computing, Applied Science Private University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/DrMahmoudAljawarneh/failsafe-caci-iot"
url: "https://github.com/DrMahmoudAljawarneh/failsafe-caci-iot"
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-11-13
abstract: >-
  Simulator, frozen 800-run experiment matrix, and manuscript source for a
  fail-safe context-adaptive access-control design for cyber-physical IoT. The
  design separates optimisable adaptation inside an admissible set from the
  unconditional actuation and safety invariants that define the set, and
  evaluates the separation under adaptive context poisoning.
keywords:
  - context-adaptive access control
  - Internet of Things
  - cyber-physical systems
  - safety invariants
  - Bayesian belief updating
  - fail-safe enforcement
